   "subject": "Implementing CCA as a SEM",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hello,</div><div><br></div><div>for a project I am trying to conduct Canonical Correlation Analysis (CCA) with incomplete data. I found this paper (<a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-01310-3_22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-01310-3_22&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792417347687000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1n6qP9WpfajNzEaX1-Cxva\">https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-01310-3_22</a>) formulating CCA using SEM. However, I know nothing about SEM and how to specify models and am somewhat confused looking through resources for the last few days. I&#39;d appreciate any pointers on how the proposed method could be implemented using lavaan.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you for any help on this!<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
